    <statement><p>Given <m>f(x,y)=7xy^{3}-8x^{6}y</m>. Compute:</p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial^2f}{\partial{x}^2}=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>\frac{\partial^2f}{\partial{y}^2}=</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-240x^{4}y</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>42xy</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\frac{\partial{f}}{\partial{x}}</m> and <m>\frac{\partial{f}}{\partial{y}}</m>



<m>\frac{\partial{f}}{\partial{x}}=7y^{3}-48x^{5}y \qquad \frac{\partial{f}}{\partial{y}}=21xy^{2}-8x^{6}</m>



We now differentiate <m>\frac{\partial{f}}{\partial{x}}</m> with respect to <m>x</m> and <m>\frac{\partial{f}}{\partial{y}}</m> with respect to <m>y</m>. We get



<m>\frac{\partial^2f}{\partial{x}^2}=\frac{\partial{f}}{\partial{x}}f_x=-240x^{4}y \qquad \frac{\partial^2f}{\partial{y}^2}=\frac{\partial{f}}{\partial{y}}f_y=42xy</m>





</solution>
